  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A staggered conformation is a chemical conformation of an ethane-like molecule in which the substituents are at the maximum distance from each other. This requires the torsional angle to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/694138fb-3c53-4a2e-bf01-c0c8c3fb1f18-image.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 196px;\" /></p><p>In anti conformation the dihedral angle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>180</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math> (maximum)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
